 "summary": "The general criterion is stated in terms of `Even ((finrank K V).choose 2)` for arbitrary even positive dimension and the dimension-four and dimension-six readings are thin corollaries of it, so there is no special-case duplication. Every hypothesis (`NeZero (2 : K)`, `Q.Nondegenerate`, `Even (finrank K V)`, `0 < finrank K V`) is used and necessary \u2014 the forall-version is false in odd dimension three and the dimension-four version is false for `Q = 0`.",
